    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d586">

                <pb facs="0779" n="697" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg697"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The United States Minister in Paris to the Minister of
                        Foreign Affairs.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-09-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 12, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have received the note which your
                    excellency wrote to me on the 7th ultimo in answer to a communication I had the
                    honor to address you on the 1st of said month, with respect to the alleged
                    projects of Dr. Gwin and his associates in Mexico.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to transmit to your excellency the enclosed copy of a despatch
                    which I have just received from my government.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of this occasion, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN BIGELOW.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>For enclosure see Mr. Seward’s despatch to Mr. Bigelow, No. 231, August 24,
                        1865, page—.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
